.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH taur-git-serve 1  "taur-git-serve " 
.SH NAME
taur\-git\-serve \- aurweb\-style SSH command handler. Reads `SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND`
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaur git\-serve\fR [\fB\-\-home\fR] <\fB\-\-user\fR> [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
aurweb\-style SSH command handler. Reads `SSH_ORIGINAL_COMMAND`.
.PP
OpenSSH forces this via the `command=` option printed by `ssh\-auth`. The account comes from `\-\-user` (the key lookup), not from the SSH login name.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
Data directory (default: ~/.local/share/taur)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fI<USER>\fR
Account that owns the key OpenSSH accepted
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Command\-line flags take precedence over environment variables, which take precedence over defaults.
.TP
\fBTAUR_HOME\fR
Data directory (database, git repos, outbox, SSH host key). Default: ~/.local/share/taur.
